WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Tesla spent $4.73 billion last quarter, mostly on vehicle and energy production capacity. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 648. Cybercab Battery Design, Texas Robotaxi Registrations, Waymo's New Coverage, then First Principles. Tesla built the Cybercab Battery Pack with spare room to switch to LFP cells later. Tesla Rodi reports, the pack uses four individually sealed modules instead of a single structural block. Robert Sumpf, director of Mechanical

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.040
design engineering for battery modules and packs, said the space allows more lower density

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.840
LFP cells to maintain range while cutting costs and improving cycle life.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.160
Lars Moravie noted part of the space exists because fewer batteries were needed than initially

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:45.720
planned.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.620
The design targets service ability for vehicles expected to accumulate high mileage.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.800
The cyber cab line at Giga Texas is now outpacing Robotaxi deployments.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:02.981
Texas now lists an authorized Robotaxi fleet of 1,051 vehicles, according to TradingView.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:08.001
544 of those are Cybercabs, and 507 are Model-wise.

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.381
Cybercabs now represent 52% of the fleet.

00:01:11.921 --> 00:01:18.481
As recently as early October, the registry showed roughly 319 Cybercabs against 420 Model-wise.

00:01:18.921 --> 00:01:22.081
The company plans to add Cybercabs in Dallas next month.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:28.061
The DMV data shows only authorized vehicles and does not confirm active passenger operations.

00:01:28.681 --> 00:01:34.321
Tesla operates robotaxies in Austin, Houston, and Dallas, and Texas, and in parts of Florida.

00:01:35.464 --> 00:01:41.144
Waymo is expanding its driverless service area by nearly 250 square miles, electric reports.

00:01:41.644 --> 00:01:47.884
The additions span Los Angeles, Nashville, Orlando, San Diego, and the San Francisco Bay area.

00:01:47.884 --> 00:01:52.164
The new zones connect neighborhoods and transit points and markets where the service

00:01:52.164 --> 00:01:57.344
already runs without drivers. Los Angeles coverage now reaches the South Bay through Manhattan

00:01:57.344 --> 00:02:03.564
Beach and Radondo Beach to Torrance. Nashville coverage extends to the zoo, and San Diego now

00:02:03.564 --> 00:02:09.944
includes LaHoya, University City, and Claremont. The Bay Area expansion reaches San Jose and Campbell,

00:02:10.464 --> 00:02:16.348
and adds a Bart connection at Berriessa Station. Formula One World Champion Damon Hill wrote

00:02:16.348 --> 00:02:20.908
in a Tesla cyber cab in Austin, according to the Tesla Motors community on Reddit.

00:02:21.408 --> 00:02:26.068
It was his first cyber cab ride. Gary Black warned Tesla bulls against assuming

00:02:26.068 --> 00:02:31.928
Robotaxi dominance, Benzinga reports. He cited competition from Chinese EV makers.

00:02:33.032 --> 00:02:37.692
Tesla is recruiting five positions in Vietnam, covering sales, service, charging,

00:02:38.092 --> 00:02:44.232
human resources, and purchasing, according to TN Global. Ricky Ipp announced the roles on X and

00:02:44.232 --> 00:02:48.992
and stated the mission is to build a world of amazing abundance. Tesla established Tesla

00:02:48.992 --> 00:02:55.512
Motors Vietnam LLC in September, with charter capital of 77.667 billion Vietnamese

00:02:55.512 --> 00:03:01.712
dong, or $3 million, and headquarters in Ho Chi Minh City. Registered activities include

00:03:01.712 --> 00:03:06.952
wholesale and retail sales of vehicles, parts, machinery, and equipment, along with import,

00:03:07.212 --> 00:03:12.472
export, and distribution. None of the postings describe factory or manufacturing activities.

00:03:12.472 --> 00:03:18.032
The Filing's lists sales, service, site development, administration, and regional sourcing.

00:03:18.592 --> 00:03:26.272
Vietnam's car market reached 48,484 units sold in August, with Vin Fast holding 42% share.

00:03:27.378 --> 00:03:32.778
A Tesla semi-Lithium battery caught fire on Interstate 880 in California, notebook check

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:33.198
reports.

00:03:33.838 --> 00:03:35.198
The driver escaped the vehicle.

00:03:35.758 --> 00:03:39.218
CHP estimated the fire could burn for 15 to 18 hours.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:44.809
The incident shut down the interstate while responders managed the blaze. BlackRock's

00:03:44.809 --> 00:03:54.949
schedule 13G slash A filing shows it held $196,348,742 Tesla shares as of September 30. Tesla

00:03:54.949 --> 00:04:01.529
Roddy noted from the filing. That equals 4.96% of the company. The firm reported sole voting

00:04:01.529 --> 00:04:13.249
power over 180,605,472 shares, and sold dispositive power over all 196,348,742 shares.

00:04:13.789 --> 00:04:16.949
BlackRock stated it holds the position as a passive investment.

00:04:17.529 --> 00:04:21.589
No single BlackRock client or fund owns more than 5% on its own.

00:04:22.525 --> 00:04:27.905
The filing marks the 4th amendment to the original schedule, and the move below the 5% threshold

00:04:27.905 --> 00:04:30.625
ends the requirement for further updates on this holding.

00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:36.545
Korea and police have charged 80 Tesla drivers for using illegal devices to unlock full self-driving

00:04:36.545 --> 00:04:42.548
or FSD features, electric reports. Tesla's official account posted the message,

00:04:43.108 --> 00:04:46.908
what goes up must come down. The short statement appeared without additional

00:04:46.908 --> 00:04:52.728
context or explanation. New Tesla vehicles can now supply power to tools and devices through the

00:04:52.728 --> 00:04:57.968
charge port using the Gen 3 mobile connector under power share, according to the Tesla Motors'

00:04:57.968 --> 00:05:04.521
community on Reddit. Canada is excluded from the rollout. Tesla told Sandy Monroe in early

00:05:04.521 --> 00:05:11.081
2025 that it was targeting a cyber cab pack under 50 kilowatt hours with close to 300 miles of

00:05:11.081 --> 00:05:16.341
range. That figure sits under a chemistry choice the company has not locked for the life of the car.

00:05:17.041 --> 00:05:24.141
LFP cells cost less, generate less heat, and tolerate more charge cycles than the nickel-based 4680 cells

00:05:24.141 --> 00:05:29.601
currently installed. Reserved internal volume is there so a lower density chemistry can still

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:35.221
meet that range target as production scales. The trade is a modest reduction in cell volume in

00:05:35.221 --> 00:05:41.301
exchange for replacing one module without discarding the entire pack. Eric Ehrlich said replacing

00:05:41.301 --> 00:05:46.721
an entire pack before half a million miles is a killer on cost. Swapping a single module

00:05:46.721 --> 00:05:51.541
keeps the vehicle in service and spreads the battery's capital cost across more revenue miles.

00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:56.041
full-pack replacement before that half million mile mark would erase much of the

00:05:56.041 --> 00:06:01.561
per mile savings high utilization is supposed to deliver. Adding extra LFP cells

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:05.541
to offset lower energy density still keeps total pack costs lower than a

00:06:05.541 --> 00:06:09.581
denser chemistry that cannot be serviced in the field. Over the life of the

00:06:09.581 --> 00:06:13.621
vehicle savings on replacement cycles and less downtime matter more than the

00:06:13.621 --> 00:06:18.661
marginal range lost on any single trip. The same logic applies whether Tesla owns

00:06:18.661 --> 00:06:20.361
the car or a fleet customer does.

00:06:20.921 --> 00:06:25.641
The architecture embeds a bet that utilization, not peak energy density, is the dominant

00:06:25.641 --> 00:06:28.021
variable in Robotaxi unit economics.

